#!args scenario=Scenario_OneRound seed=42
#
# Germany opens by building an army, then the round is passed out.
# Run:  tests/run-cli.sh tests/qgc/opening_turn.qgc
#
# NOTE ON ORDERING: `assert` reads state the moment it runs, and the game boots asynchronously.
# Only the answer commands (`prompt`, `play`, `select`, `pass`) wait for the game to reach a
# prompt — so put a `prompt` first to synchronise, or your assertions read the pre-game state.

# Every faction is dealt OpeningHandSize and must discard OpeningDiscardCount before the first turn
# starts, so six mandatory discard prompts arrive ahead of anything else. Auto-answering takes the
# first three cards of each hand (PassMode.NotAllowed), which is deterministic under the seed above.
auto 6

prompt                      # blocks until the first prompt: turn 1, Germany, PLAY_CARD

assert turn == 1
assert faction == GERMANY
assert step == PLAY_CARD

# Dealt OpeningHandSize and cut back to HandSize, the three cards landing in the discard pile.
# opening_discard_disabled.qgc pins the other side of this branch.
assert handsize GERMANY == 7
assert discardsize GERMANY == 3

# Hand contents depend on the start-of-game deck shuffle, so this index is pinned to the seed in
# the #!args line above. Under seed=42 the prompt lists Build Army first.
play 1                      # Build Army
select 1                    # first legal country
assert handsize GERMANY == 6

# Nobody contests the rest of the round.
auto 40
assert round == 1
quit
